</section>
<section aria-labelledby="tablet-h">
  <h2 id="tablet-h" class="type-h2">Tablet</h2>
  <p>From 768 to 1023px the row sits on the 8-column grid with 16px gutters and is 736px wide with its 16px side padding. The title takes columns 1 to 4, the category columns 5 and 6, and the arrow cell columns 7 and 8, right-aligned. An unlocked row is 104px tall. The frame below is 768px wide, so it shows the tablet layout on any screen.</p>
  <figure class="preview-frame">
    <div class="preview-frame__scroller" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="List row at tablet width, scrollable">
      <iframe src="/previews/list-row/" width="768" height="460" title="List row at tablet width" loading="lazy"></iframe>
    </div>
    <figcaption class="preview-frame__caption type-small">Two rows and a locked row at 768px. Hover and focus work in the frame.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p>In a locked row the lock takes the arrow's place and the helper line sits under it in columns 7 and 8, where it wraps to two lines. The title and category are centered against both, and the row is 144px tall.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="use-h">
  <h2 id="use-h" class="type-h2">Using the list row</h2>
  <div class="rules">
    <div class="rule"><h3 class="type-h3">Do</h3><ul>
      <li>Use it on the page surface, with a rule between rows.</li>
      <li>Hide the arrow from screen readers (<code>aria-hidden</code>); the title is the link name.</li>
    </ul></div>
    <div class="rule"><h3 class="type-h3">Don't</h3><ul>
      <li>Put a row inside a tinted section. The hover tint would disappear.</li>
      <li>Add a button to the row. The row is the target.</li>
    </ul></div>
  </div>
</section>
